From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: enc: fix the v4l2-compliance failures

v4l2-compliance 1.32 on the encoder node (runner job 34) failed four
tests:

- VIDIOC_TRY_FMT and VIDIOC_S_FMT on the CAPTURE queue: the tool sends a
  format of all ones and the coded size 0xffffffff, aligned up to 256,
  wrapped to 0 ("!pix.sizeimage"). Clamp the coded size to 64 MiB, which
  also keeps the stream size in bits that the engine takes within 32 bits.

- VIDIOC_(UN)SUBSCRIBE_EVENT: V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_OUTPUT is only
  defined for stateful encoders; nothing reads it here, so drop it. The
  encoder has 20 controls.

- VIDIOC_G/S_PARM: the tool allows the frame rate ioctls on an M2M node
  only for stateful encoders. The stateless encode uAPI relies on them for
  the frame rate the core puts in the SPS and uses for its rate control,
  like the Hantro encoder of the same series; the tool predates that uAPI.
  Keep them, documented, as the one expected failure.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a2/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.c
+++ b2/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.c
@@ -238,16 +238,6 @@
 		},
 		.capabilities	= CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_H264_ENC,
 	},
-	{
-		.cfg = {
-			.id	= V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_OUTPUT,
-			.min	= 1,
-			.max	= 32,
-			.step	= 1,
-			.def	= 1,
-		},
-		.capabilities	= CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_H264_ENC,
-	},
 };
 
 const unsigned int cedrus_enc_controls_count = ARRAY_SIZE(cedrus_enc_controls);
@@ -304,7 +294,8 @@
 	if (!sizeimage)
 		sizeimage = raw_fmt->bytesperline * raw_fmt->height * 3 / 2;
 
-	sizeimage = max_t(unsigned int, sizeimage, CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_MIN_SIZE);
+	sizeimage = clamp_t(unsigned int, sizeimage, CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_MIN_SIZE,
+			    CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_MAX_SIZE);
 	pix_fmt->sizeimage = ALIGN(sizeimage, CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_ALIGN);
 
 	pix_fmt->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
@@ -459,7 +450,13 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-/* The frame rate goes to the VUI timing info of the SPS. */
+/*
+ * The frame rate goes to the VUI timing info of the SPS and to the encode
+ * core's rate control, as the stateless encode uAPI asks (the Hantro
+ * encoder of the same series does the same). v4l2-compliance up to 1.32
+ * predates that uAPI and reports G/S_PARM on a node it does not classify
+ * as a stateful encoder as a failure: that one is expected.
+ */
 static int cedrus_enc_g_parm(struct file *file, void *priv,
 			     struct v4l2_streamparm *parm)
 {
--- a2/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.h
+++ b2/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.h
@@ -47,6 +47,8 @@
 #define CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_ALIGN			256
 /* The stream size register counts in units of 65536 bits (0x12011). */
 #define CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_MIN_SIZE		SZ_64K
+/* Keeps the stream size in bits (VE_ENC_AVC_STM_BIT_MAX) within 32 bits. */
+#define CEDRUS_ENC_CODED_MAX_SIZE		SZ_64M
 
 /* P pictures narrower than 13 macroblocks never finish on the H616. */
 #define CEDRUS_ENC_INTER_MIN_WIDTH_MBS		13
